---
import ContentPage from "../layouts/ContentPage.astro";
import { ORG_EMAIL } from "../lib/seo";

const site = "https://refocus.co.in";
const UPDATED = "2026-09-28";
const mailto = `mailto:${ORG_EMAIL}`;
const title = "Terms & Conditions";
const description =
  "The terms for using Refocus on the web and on iPhone, including accounts, community rules, and the Apple App Store license.";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: "Terms & Conditions — Refocus",
    url: `${site}/terms`,
    description,
    dateModified: new Date(UPDATED).toISOString(),
  },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="/terms"
  heading="Terms & Conditions"
  updated={UPDATED}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") are an agreement between you and
    Refocus. They cover the Refocus iOS app, the website
    (<a href="https://refocus.co.in">refocus.co.in</a>), and the product
    (<a href="https://dashboard.refocus.co.in">dashboard.refocus.co.in</a>)
    (together, the "Service"). By creating an account or using the Service, you
    agree to these Terms and to the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If
    you do not agree, do not use Refocus.
  </p>

  <p class="contact-lead">
    Questions about these Terms? Email
    <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    Refocus is a focus room: you book a session, get paired with someone else
    who is there to work, and can join a live video call. The Service is free.
    There are no purchases or subscriptions in the app. If that changes, we
    will show the price and terms before you pay.
  </p>

  <h2>Accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 13 years old.</li>
    <li>If you are under the age of majority where you live, a parent or guardian must agree to these Terms for you.</li>
    <li>You must give accurate account information and keep your sign-in secure.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for activity on your account.</li>
    <li>You can sign in with email, Google, or Sign in with Apple.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can delete your account in the iOS app under Settings → Danger zone →
    Delete account, or in Settings on the website. You can also email
    <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a> from the address on the account. Deletion
    is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Sessions, chat, and community posts are shared with other people. You agree
    not to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Harass, threaten, or abuse anyone.</li>
    <li>Post illegal, hateful, or sexually explicit content.</li>
    <li>Impersonate another person or collect their information without consent.</li>
    <li>Disrupt, reverse-engineer, or overload the Service.</li>
    <li>Break the law or someone else's rights.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    There is no tolerance for objectionable content or abusive users. You can
    block and report people in the product. We may remove content and suspend
    or terminate accounts that break these Terms. To report something you
    cannot flag in the product, email <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of what you post, including messages and check-in notes.
    You give Refocus a limited license to host, display, and process that
    content only to operate the Service — for example, to show a message to the
    person you sent it to, or a check-in to your session partner.
  </p>

  <h2>iPhone and iPad</h2>
  <p>
    If you download Refocus from the Apple App Store, this section also applies.
    If it conflicts with the rest of these Terms, this section controls for
    that download.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      These Terms are between you and Refocus only, not with Apple. Apple is
      not responsible for the app or its content.
    </li>
    <li>
      The app is licensed, not sold. The license is non-exclusive and
      non-transferable. You may use it on Apple-branded devices that you own or
      control, as allowed by the Usage Rules in the Apple Media Services Terms
      and Conditions.
    </li>
    <li>
      Refocus is solely responsible for maintenance and support. Contact
      <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      If the app fails to conform to an applicable warranty, you may notify
      Apple, and Apple may refund the purchase price, if any. To the maximum
      extent permitted by law, Apple has no other warranty obligation for the
      app. Any other claim, loss, liability, damage, cost, or expense
      attributable to a failure to conform to a warranty is Refocus's
      responsibility.
    </li>
    <li>
      Refocus, not Apple, is responsible for claims relating to the app,
      including product-liability claims, claims that the app fails to conform
      to a legal or regulatory requirement, and claims under consumer
      protection or similar law.
    </li>
    <li>
      Refocus, not Apple, is responsible for the investigation, defense,
      settlement, and discharge of any third-party claim that the app, or your
      possession and use of it, infringes that third party's intellectual
      property rights.
    </li>
    <li>
      You represent that you are not located in a country subject to a U.S.
      Government embargo, and that you are not listed on any U.S. Government
      list of prohibited or restricted parties.
    </li>
    <li>
      You must also comply with applicable third-party terms when using the
      app, including your wireless-data agreement.
    </li>
    <li>
      Apple and Apple's subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these
      Terms. After you accept them, Apple has the right to enforce them against
      you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Service availability</h2>
  <p>
    Refocus is provided as is and as available. Features can change, and the
    Service can be interrupted. We do not promise that it will be uninterrupted
    or error-free.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Live video, sign-in, email, and analytics are provided by other companies.
    Their terms can apply when you use those features. The
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> lists them.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, Refocus is not liable for indirect,
    incidental, or consequential damages, or for loss of data or profits,
    arising from your use of the Service.
  </p>

  <h2>Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using Refocus and delete your account at any time. We may
    suspend or end access if you break these Terms or misuse the Service.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms. The "Last updated" date above is the current
    version. If you keep using Refocus after an update, you accept the new
    Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>, or the
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
